## Evidence (dotnet mesh unwind, `doc/plan/c016-worklog/stage2-dotnet-mesh-unwind-summary.md` B1)
With the framework's physical settlement removed, two .NET MeshNodes that connect to each other at the same time (manual
bilateral / caller-first) produce, in `ZLINK_ROUTER_DEBUG=1`: `router identify_peer: replace duplicate ... existing_local=0
new_local=0` — Core treated the reciprocal collision as a SAME-direction replacement (both pipes seen as non-local /
inbound?) rather than the opposite-direction collapse D-B96 tested with sequential connects. Consequence: the reply to an
application request is lost and the caller sees TimedOut(101) even after an explicit resend; 4 Stateful tests + 1 Canonical
test red.

